{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And of the precious things of the earth.</b> After he mentioned the fruits of the mountains, he mentioned the fruits of the lowland. And in the word ״ומלואה״ — 'and its fullness' — are included silver and gold and all minerals and the rest of all the acquisitions of the earth, for everything is in it, and it is blessed by the good will of the Holy One, blessed be He, who dwelt in the bush." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> 'Blessed of YHWH be his land' — why was Joseph blessed with the blessing of the land more than all the tribes? Because the first man, who hearkened to the voice of his wife, caused the earth to be cursed on his account, as it is said (Genesis 3): ״כי שמעת לקול אשתך״ — 'because you hearkened to the voice of your wife,' etc. Joseph, who did not hearken to his master's wife, caused the earth to be blessed on his account; as it is written: 'Blessed of YHWH be his land.'" "<b>Let his produce come to the head of Joseph.</b> This blessing — and the word is unusual, and it is compounded from באתה and from תבא — and Moses hinted to him here: just as you came into the exile of Egypt before your brothers, so shall you come to redemption before them; and they are forty-five years that the exiled ones are destined to be redeemed before the scattered ones, and between redemption and redemption, forty-five years."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:54:11.891096779Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}